--- Schema (amazon_reviews/toponymy_erasure) ---

Facet 0: review_sentiment (categorical)
  Captures the overall sentiment polarity expressed by the reviewer toward the product, ranging from enthusiastic praise to strong dissatisfaction.
  - highly_positive
  - mostly_positive
  - mixed
  - mostly_negative
  - highly_negative
  - Other

Facet 1: review_focus_aspect (categorical)
  Captures the primary product attribute or dimension the reviewer focuses on when evaluating the product.
  - fit_and_sizing
  - durability_and_construction
  - material_and_texture
  - ease_of_use
  - value_for_price
  - aesthetics_and_appearance
  - content_and_storytelling
  - performance_and_functionality
  - Other

Facet 2: reviewer_experience_stage (categorical)
  Captures the stage of the product ownership lifecycle that the reviewer is describing, from pre-purchase expectations through long-term use or eventual failure/return.
  - pre_purchase_expectations
  - unboxing_and_first_impressions
  - initial_use
  - extended_use
  - post_failure_or_return
  - Other

